{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-09353009-2aa1-4a66-b383-0d3f21973219","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d4318f3732f1b24","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-m9mmtgr5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md","content":"# Keyboard accessibility remediation for four audited Dashboard flows\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the accessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion, all four flows are fully operable with keyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and consistent visible focus indicators.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Fix all keyboard-operability defects enumerated in the accessibility audit for the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission), including:\n  - Focus traps in modals — focus must enter, move within, escape (dismiss/confirm), and return correctly for every modal in the audited flows.\n  - Unreachable controls — every interactive control in the audited flows must be reachable and operable via keyboard (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the pattern requires it, Enter/Space/Escape activation).\n- Make focus indicators consistent and clearly visible across the audited flows, matching the Dashboard's component library focus styling so indicator presentation no longer varies between flows.\n- Out of scope per the strategy: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones. Where a keyboard fix incidentally improves semantics, that is acceptable; no separate semantics work is in scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using keyboard alone, verified against the audit report's per-flow defect list with every enumerated defect resolved or explicitly waived with rationale.\n- No focus traps remain: for every modal exercised in the audited flows, focus can be moved into, within, and out of the modal, and focus returns to the invoking control on close.\n- Every interactive control in the audited flows is reachable and operable by keyboard.\n- Visible focus indicators are present and stylistically consistent across all controls in the audited flows.\n- Pointer-based interaction with the four flows shows no regression from these changes.\n- The Dashboard build pipeline is green with these changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23855,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aed50cdb238dbf4f","agent_id":"a33932ddfb1f94c5e","session_id":"e9284ab1-017b-48c0-9b38-20475332623f","uuid":"e6ef2f05-1b37-4394-9335-9595c7f0c2f7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:56:48.839Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
