{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a33932ddfb1f94c5e","run_id":"0mvl9t3gp-b6989de8","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aed50cdb238dbf4f","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-h5-l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn-T-epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-m9mmtgr5/e9284ab1-017b-48c0-9b38-20475332623f/tasks/a33932ddfb1f94c5e.output","summary":"Sanity checks done: batch-read confirms both epic files match the summary plan (dependencies, priority, type, HLR mappings), the contract validator printed `OK: contract checks passed for RHAISTRAT-9017`, and `decompose_complete=true` is now set as the final action.\n\nDecomposition of RHAISTRAT-9017 (keyboard accessibility conformance for core Dashboard flows) is complete:\n\n- Triage: not below-threshold (two distinct work streams — Dashboard code fixes plus substantive VPAT/accessibility-statement authoring — across two components); not docs-only.\n- Two epics with a single-edge DAG: `RHAISTRAT-9017-E001` (Implementation, Dashboard, RHOAI Dashboard, P1, covers HLR-1 and HLR-2 bundled as one remediation pass over the same four flows, rationale recorded in the traceability matrix) → `RHAISTRAT-9017-E002` (Implementation, Documentation, docs-authoring, P2 per the docs-authoring priority exception, covers HLR-3, Rule 11 edge).\n- No Investigation epics — the strategy states there are no open questions and the audit enumerates the defects.\n- Health warnings recorded: missing strategy sections (teams/dependencies/ACs/NFRs), assumed Documentation owner team, and a re-split trigger for E001 if the audit defect volume exceeds a sprint.\n\nArtifacts:\n- /private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-m9mmtgr5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-decomposition.md\n- /private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-m9mmtgr5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md (+ RHAISTRAT-9017-E001-ai-signals.md)\n- /private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621q