e four flows and the same UI surfaces (modals, forms, controls). Splitting would produce two epics editing the same components and flows — not separately schedulable. |\n40\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | VPAT and accessibility statement update and republication, with technical review (docs-authoring epic; priority P2 per docs-authoring exception — strategy priority Normal). |\n41\t\n42\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-1 and HLR-2 are consolidated into one epic: they describe the same remediation pass over the same component, team, and flows (the audit's defect list mixes focus-trap, reachability, and focus-indicator findings per flow), so they are one capability per the consolidation rule.\n43\t\n44\t## Health Warnings\n45\t\n46\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria section, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs, problem statement, and audit reference; per-epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR wording. The audit report itself (exact defect list per flow) is referenced but not embedded in the strategy.\n47\t- **Team assumption**: the strategy names no owner for the Documentation component; the documentation epic is assigned to \"RHOAI Documentation\" by convention. The Dashboard epic's team (RHOAI Dashboard) is corroborated by the architecture context file for Dashboard.\n48\t- **Potential scope trap**: HLR-3's \"republished\" wording implies a publication process whose cadence is outside engineering control; the docs epic's AC is written on the deliverable (updated, reviewed, submitted-for-republication content), with publication timing noted as a risk on that epic.\n49\t- **Epic size / re-split trigger**: E001 remediates all enumerated defects across four flows in one logical change (a single remediation pass over the Dashboard's shared modal/form/focus surface). If the audit defect volume exceeds roughly one sprint of effort, re-split E001 by audited flow (one epic per flow) — the fixes are per-flow independent and share only the component surface.\n50\t\n51\t## Tiered Delivery\n52\t\n53\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; the only edge is the internal docs-after-implementation ordering.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bd74f50285c7495","agent_id":"a81e9189fc6b5ff0d","session_id":"e9284ab1-017b-48c0-9b38-20475332623f","uuid":"92275ed8-fa9f-442a-8d47-697dea179ba0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:57:56.344Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c9026f550d9f89b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
